// zhao_shell_v2_lease_path.vlt -- inherited-warning waivers, scoped BY FILE.
//
// The lease-path harness now composes `zhao_geom_bin_pipe_v2`, which drags in
// the whole V3 texture closure. Linting that closure at `-Wall` produces 113
// warnings -- 89 UNUSEDSIGNAL, 17 UNUSEDPARAM, 4 PINCONNECTEMPTY, and one each
// of SYNCASYNCNET, UNDRIVEN and DECLFILENAME.
//
// NONE OF THEM ARE THIS HARNESS'S, and that was measured rather than assumed:
// the identical set appears when `tests/geometry/tb_geom_bin_pipe_v2.sv` is
// linted the same way, and nothing in the tree lints that closure at `-Wall`
// today, so they have simply never been surfaced.
//
// WHY A .vlt AND NOT `-Wno-UNUSEDSIGNAL` ON THE COMMAND LINE. A blanket
// suppression would also hide the next unused signal somebody leaves in the
// HARNESS, which is the one file this test exists to keep clean. Waiving by
// file keeps `-Wall` strict where it can be met and silent only where the
// warnings were inherited. If the V3 closure is ever cleaned up, deleting lines
// from here is how that progress becomes visible.
//
// This is a WAIVER, not a fix. The warnings are real and they belong to their
// own packets.
// A NOTE ON THE GLOBS. Verilator reports Windows paths with MIXED
// separators -- `fpga/rtl/texture\zhao_texture_island_v3_top.sv` -- so a
// pattern with a forward slash before the basename matches NOTHING, and a
// waiver that matches nothing is perfectly silent about being useless. The
// first version of this file had exactly that and the warnings all came
// back. Separator-agnostic prefixes only.
//
// AND THAT FIX WAS ONLY HALF A FIX, found 2026-09-19. The separator before
// the BASENAME was made agnostic and the ones inside the DIRECTORY were left
// as forward slashes, so these globs match only when the CALLER happens to
// pass posix paths. design/fit_targets.yml does, which is why this looked
// settled; tools/budget/completion_register.py's closure_paths() hands back
// Windows backslash paths, and linting from it brings all 112 texture-subtree
// warnings back -- in a subtree the caller never touched, looking exactly like
// a regression they just caused. That is the same failure the paragraph above
// describes, one directory level up.
//
// `?` matches a single character in Verilator's globs, so `*fpga?rtl?texture*`
// matches both spellings and cannot rot this way again. Proven by running the
// baseline twice, once with posix paths and once with backslash paths: both
// silent, RC 0.
`verilator_config

lint_off -rule UNUSEDSIGNAL    -file "*fpga?rtl?texture*"
lint_off -rule UNUSEDSIGNAL    -file "*fpga?rtl?raster*"
lint_off -rule UNUSEDSIGNAL    -file "*fpga?rtl?geometry*"
lint_off -rule UNUSEDSIGNAL    -file "*fpga?rtl?common*"
lint_off -rule UNUSEDSIGNAL    -file "*fpga?rtl?video*"

lint_off -rule UNUSEDPARAM     -file "*fpga?rtl?texture*"
lint_off -rule UNUSEDPARAM     -file "*fpga?rtl?raster*"
lint_off -rule UNUSEDPARAM     -file "*fpga?rtl?geometry*"
lint_off -rule UNUSEDPARAM     -file "*fpga?rtl?common*"

lint_off -rule PINCONNECTEMPTY -file "*fpga?rtl?texture*"
lint_off -rule UNDRIVEN        -file "*fpga?rtl?texture*"
lint_off -rule DECLFILENAME    -file "*zhao_render_texture_pkg.sv"

// The one warning Verilator attributes to the harness rather than the closure.
// Its `rst_n` port is flopped asynchronously here and synchronously somewhere
// inside the V3 closure, and the report lands on the port declaration. The
// identical warning lands on `tb_geom_bin_pipe_v2.sv:11` for the same reason,
// which is what says it is inherited: this harness's own always_ff blocks are
// all async-reset, and the assertion block that used to read `rst_n`
// synchronously was removed earlier for exactly this rule.
lint_off -rule SYNCASYNCNET    -file "*zhao_shell_v2_lease_path.sv"
lint_off -rule SYNCASYNCNET    -file "*zhao_shell_top_v2.sv"
// THE CONNECTED TOP, and the attribution was MEASURED rather than assumed.
// `zhao_console_core` instantiates `zhao_shell_top_v2`, so it inherits the
// same warning at its own `rst_n` port declaration. The test that says it is
// inherited: every one of that file's three `always_ff` blocks was rewritten
// to a SYNCHRONOUS reset in a scratchpad copy and linted, and the warning came
// back unchanged. A warning that survives the removal of this file's only
// asynchronous flops is not this file's warning. The async form is kept
// because it is the house style and because a synchronous-reset glue flop
// beside asynchronously-reset blocks is a real reset-domain hazard, not a
// lint preference.
lint_off -rule SYNCASYNCNET    -file "*zhao_console_core.sv"
// THE PAIRED DIFFERENTIAL, same reason as the two above and no more than that.
// Its verdict flops -- the sticky mismatch bit, the toggle witness -- reset on
// `negedge rst_n` while the shells beneath it also read `rst_n` synchronously,
// so the harness inherits the warning from the thing it is measuring rather
// than introducing a new one. The mutant copy gets it too or its control fails
// for the wrong reason, which would read as "the mutant fired".
lint_off -rule SYNCASYNCNET    -file "*zhao_shell_paired_diff.sv"
lint_off -rule SYNCASYNCNET    -file "*zhao_shell_paired_diff_mutant.sv"

// The V1 shell lints CLEAN at -Wall with no SYNCASYNCNET, which is how the
// sibling's copy is attributed: the warning arrives with the V3 closure that
// the bin-pipe swap pulls in, not with anything zhao_shell_top_v2.sv writes.
// Measured, not assumed -- `verilator --lint-only -Wall --top-module
// zhao_shell_top` is silent.
//
// Both files take their waivers from THIS file rather than each keeping a
// copy, because two copies of a waiver drift and the drift is silent.
